-- T0284
{id="t0284-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="At dusk: rinsed gloves",body="My note from at dusk: the field trial crew carried rinsed gloves. my brother started coughing. I had not yet heard that the siren began.",anchor={scene="RBBarn"}},
{id="t0284-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Count the calves as absent",body="I told them the barn was empty after the morning count. It was true if you counted people. The two calves were still there, and I could hear the smaller one pressing its head against the gate whenever a truck stopped outside.\n\nA man I had never seen asked for the ledger, then asked whether I kept another. I said the kitchen calendar had the births on it. He took that too. By evening the gate had a new chain. Nobody asked me to feed them, and nobody said I could go back in.\n\nI left the milk pail by the door because I thought a person who came to lock it would see it. In the morning the pail was gone. The chain was still there.",anchor={scene="RBBarn"}},
-- T0285
{id="t0285-01",kind="set",pieces={"FirstAidKit","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Clouded sample jar by the cab",body="The pair is streaked with clouded sample jar from treated rows. It was set aside after the flies vanished, before anyone marked the cab unsafe.",anchor={scene="RBBurnt"}},
{id="t0285-02",kind="set",pieces={"FirstAidKit","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A waterline after the fire",body="The kit is unopened. The water bottle has a black line drawn halfway down it and the same line repeated on the charred wall. Whoever marked it was measuring what survived the fire, not treating a burn.",anchor={scene="RBBurnt"}},
-- T0286
{id="t0286-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Near midnight: sealed seed packet",body="I kept the sealed seed packet you asked about. The trial crew passed near midnight; my brother started coughing, and only later a patrol turned everyone back.",anchor={scene="RBBurntCorpse"}},
{id="t0286-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="For the dog, if anyone asks",body="If they ask you who started it, tell them I went inside for the dog. I did. I also went back for the little box under the sink, the one with the dates written on the lid.\n\nThe men outside told me to leave it where it was. One held the door while the other watched me search. When I came out without it, they let me sit by the truck. They were careful with me then. They had already put the box in a bag of their own.\n\nThe dog came out through the back, singed and furious. Please give her water first. I don't want her remembered as another thing I left inside.",anchor={scene="RBBurntCorpse"}},
-- T0287
{id="t0287-01",kind="set",pieces={"Potato","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Marked feed sack by the kitchen chair",body="The two items are bundled beside marked feed sack; field dust lies beneath them, while a strip of road tape is caught around the bundle.",anchor={scene="RBBurntFireman"}},
{id="t0287-02",kind="set",pieces={"Potato","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Ash inside the sealed jar",body="The jar contains ash beneath its lid. A potato is wrapped in a clean bandage beside it. These were packed together before the fire spread; the jar was being carried out, while the food was left where it could be found.",anchor={scene="RBBurntFireman"}},
-- T0288
{id="t0288-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Before breakfast: rinsed gloves",body="before breakfast: the crop trial crew brought rinsed gloves. my brother started coughing. I washed everything twice before the buses quit running.",anchor={scene="RBCafe"}},
{id="t0288-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Names with breakfast",body="The woman at the next table asked why they were taking names with the breakfast order. I told her it was probably for the bill. The waitress folded the list and put it in her apron, though we had all paid at the counter.\n\nLater a man came in through the kitchen, spoke to her, and left with the folded paper. Nobody cleared our plates while he was there. I kept looking at the clock because my sister was due to meet me.\n\nShe never arrived. I wrote down the time, then crossed it out when I realized I couldn't remember whether the clock had stopped before or after the man came in. The waitress set a fresh pot on the stove and kept serving everyone else.",anchor={scene="RBCafe"}},
-- T0289
{id="t0289-01",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Clouded sample jar by the coat pocket",body="The pair is streaked with clouded sample jar from treated rows. It was set aside after the flies vanished, before anyone marked the coat pocket unsafe.",anchor={scene="RBClinic"}},
{id="t0289-02",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A dial that cannot turn",body="The battery is taped into the radio with a strip cut from a medicine label. The dial is fixed in place. The clinic kept a receiver ready on one frequency even after ordinary broadcasts had stopped.",anchor={scene="RBClinic"}},
-- T0290
{id="t0290-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Before dawn: sealed seed packet",body="My note from before dawn: the field trial crew carried sealed seed packet. my brother started coughing. I had not yet heard that the county van arrived.",anchor={scene="RBDorm"}},
{id="t0290-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Eight names on six beds",body="Room count at noon: four beds slept in, six beds assigned, eight names on the door. Nobody could explain the difference. We had made the list from the doors because the office list had been taken.\n\nA visitor came back with the office list in her hand and asked us to erase two names. She did not ask whether either student was still here. We argued about it quietly because the girl in the end bed was asleep.\n\nBy supper the visitor had gone. I wrote the two names again on a scrap and pushed it into my shoe. If somebody asks tomorrow, I can say I made a mistake. I would rather have a mistake I can show them.",anchor={scene="RBDorm"}},
-- T0291
{id="t0291-01",kind="set",pieces={"FishingRod","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Marked feed sack by the toolbox",body="The pair is streaked with marked feed sack from treated rows. It was set aside after the flies vanished, before anyone marked the toolbox unsafe.",anchor={scene="RBGunstoreSiege"}},
{id="t0291-02",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The spare receiver",body="A battery sits beside a radio whose tuning knob has been removed. The barricade can hear a single station, but no one inside can change it.",anchor={scene="RBGunstoreSiege"}},
-- T0292
{id="t0292-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Tuesday, after opening",body="Three customers from the east fields brought the same sweet chemical smell in their hair. They said the crop trial crew had sprayed before sunrise. I washed everyone twice; by noon a county van had blocked the road.",anchor={scene="RBHairSalon"}},
{id="t0292-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Appointments crossed out",body="I kept the book open so they could see when the last customer had come in. The woman asked for the names instead of the times.\n\nShe did not take the whole book. She tore out two pages and left the small notes about hair color and the money owed. One customer had asked me to call his wife. I still have her number, but I cannot remember which page it was on.\n\nWe swept after they left. A curl of paper caught under the chair and I put it here in case the customer comes back to pay.",anchor={scene="RBHairSalon"}},
-- T0293
{id="t0293-01",kind="set",pieces={"Axe","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Clouded sample jar by the counter",body="The two items are bundled beside clouded sample jar; field dust lies beneath them, while a strip of road tape is caught around the bundle.",anchor={scene="RBHeatBreakAfternoon"}},
{id="t0293-02",kind="set",pieces={"Map","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A sealed morning route",body="The map is folded to hide three streets, and the water bottle has a fresh mark for each one. Whoever drove here was counting stops before anyone on the road knew there was a route.",anchor={scene="RBHeatBreakAfternoon"}},
-- T0294
{id="t0294-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="At dusk: sealed seed packet",body="at dusk: the crop trial crew brought sealed seed packet. my brother started coughing. I washed everything twice before the siren began.",anchor={scene="RBJoanHartford"}},
{id="t0294-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The visitor list",body="They told us the list was for families. I believed them until the families arrived and nobody would let them see it.\n\nOne woman recognized a coat through the window. The man at the door said the coat belonged to a different person and closed the curtain. She waited for hours because no one would tell her whose coat she had seen.\n\nI wrote down the time they took the list. If she comes back I can at least tell her when we stopped being allowed to answer.",anchor={scene="RBJoanHartford"}},
-- T0295
{id="t0295-01",kind="set",pieces={"Mop","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Marked feed sack by the cab",body="The pair is streaked with marked feed sack from treated rows. It was set aside after the flies vanished, before anyone marked the cab unsafe.",anchor={scene="RBJudge"}},
{id="t0295-02",kind="set",pieces={"Notebook","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The second date",body="The notebook has two dates written over one another. A pencil laid across it points to the earlier entry, where the margin says that the hearing was closed before anyone arrived.",anchor={scene="RBJudge"}},
-- T0296
{id="t0296-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Near midnight: rinsed gloves",body="My note from near midnight: the field trial crew carried rinsed gloves. my brother started coughing. I had not yet heard that a patrol turned everyone back.",anchor={scene="RBLooted"}},
{id="t0296-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Things left behind the lock",body="They came while the room was still full. I thought they were stopping the stealing, but one of them knew which drawer held the names.\n\nI stood outside with a neighbor who was holding a lamp. We heard drawers open, then the men carried out one thin folder. They left the money and the jewelry where the thieves had scattered it.\n\nIn the morning the front door was broken and everyone said the folder had been stolen with the rest. I could not persuade the neighbor to say what we had seen.",anchor={scene="RBLooted"}},
-- T0297
{id="t0297-01",kind="set",pieces={"WalkieTalkie1","FirstAidKit"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Clouded sample jar by the kitchen chair",body="The pair is streaked with clouded sample jar from treated rows. It was set aside after the flies vanished, before anyone marked the kitchen chair unsafe.",anchor={scene="RBMayorWestPoint"}},
{id="t0297-02",kind="set",pieces={"Newspaper","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Two versions of the notice",body="A public notice and a pencil stub are folded together. The penciled time is earlier than the printed one, and someone has marked the first version to be collected before the doors opened.",anchor={scene="RBMayorWestPoint"}},
-- T0298
{id="t0298-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Before breakfast: sealed seed packet",body="I kept the sealed seed packet you asked about. The trial crew passed before breakfast; my brother started coughing, and only later the buses quit running.",anchor={scene="RBNolans"}},
{id="t0298-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A knock after dark",body="The first man said they were checking on us. The second asked which neighbors had left and wrote their names before he asked whether they were well.\n\nI told them the little boy next door was with his aunt. He had gone to fetch her because she was alone. When the men returned, they asked me to say that both houses had been empty since noon.\n\nI can say I misunderstood the hour. I cannot explain why they came back to change it.",anchor={scene="RBNolans"}},
-- T0299
{id="t0299-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","CannedCorn"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Marked feed sack by the coat pocket",body="The two items are bundled beside marked feed sack; field dust lies beneath them, while a strip of road tape is caught around the bundle.",anchor={scene="RBOffice"}},
{id="t0299-02",kind="set",pieces={"Sheet","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Carbon under the blotter",body="A sheet of paper has been pressed over a handwritten count. The marks beneath still show a larger number than the typed line above it. Someone saved the carbon but discarded the original.",anchor={scene="RBOffice"}},
-- T0300
{id="t0300-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Before dawn: rinsed gloves",body="before dawn: the crop trial crew brought rinsed gloves. my brother started coughing. I washed everything twice before the county van arrived.",anchor={scene="RBOther"}},
{id="t0300-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="What the messenger carried",body="He wanted the room cleared before he opened his bag. We moved the chairs into the hall and he put three envelopes on the table.\n\nThe first was for the people still here. The other two had names of places already shut. He took those away when I asked him why he had come so late.\n\nI thought he would leave a copy. Instead he asked for the empty envelopes back, too. The chairs are still in the hall because no one knows whether the room is open.",anchor={scene="RBOther"}},
-- T0301
{id="t0301-01",kind="set",pieces={"KeyRing","GardeningSprayEmpty"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Clouded sample jar by the toolbox",body="The pair is streaked with clouded sample jar from treated rows. It was set aside after the flies vanished, before anyone marked the toolbox unsafe.",anchor={scene="RBPileOCrepe"}},
-- T0302
{id="t0302-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Near lunchtime: sealed seed packet",body="My note from near lunchtime: the field trial crew carried sealed seed packet. my brother started coughing. I had not yet heard that the bridge was blocked.",anchor={scene="RBPizzaWhirled"}},
{id="t0302-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Back door count",body="At closing I counted the remaining boxes and wrote the number on the lid. A driver came for them after I had put away the register.\n\nHe had a list of addresses, but it was folded so I could only see the first. He crossed it out without unloading anything. We waited until his radio called him away.\n\nI was told to write the boxes off as spoiled. They were still warm when he took them, and I had eaten from the same batch.",anchor={scene="RBPizzaWhirled"}},
-- T0303
{id="t0303-01",kind="set",pieces={"HandShovel","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Field dust on the wash pail",body="A hand shovel rests across a wash pail, both striped with yellow dust. The pail smells of crop spray; road tape is knotted through its handle.",anchor={scene="RBPoliceSiege"}},
{id="t0303-02",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Frequency held through the siege",body="The radio dial is bound with a narrow strip of tape. Its battery has been replaced recently, although the callers barricaded here had no way to send a reply. Someone wanted them listening to one channel.",anchor={scene="RBPoliceSiege"}},
-- T0304
{id="t0304-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Prayer list, Tuesday margin",body="In the margin I wrote that the orchard hands smelled of sweet spray and asked for water before service. Their youngest began shaking before the deputy closed the lane.",anchor={scene="RBReverend"}},
{id="t0304-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A name left in the margin",body="I was asked to read the list aloud and I did. One name was missing, though the person was sitting right there. I thought the page had been copied badly.\n\nAfterward the visitor asked me not to add the name. She said another office had already settled it. The person stayed to help stack the chairs and asked why everyone had begun speaking softly.\n\nI wrote the name in the margin of my own book. It is not a record anyone will accept, but I could not bring myself to leave an empty space.",anchor={scene="RBReverend"}},
-- T0305
{id="t0305-01",kind="set",pieces={"FirstAidKit","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Seed dust under the bandages",body="A first-aid kit sits open beside a split seed sack. Yellow dust covers the gauze; black road tape is stuck to the sack.",anchor={scene="RBSWATStation"}},
{id="t0305-02",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A channel behind the lockers",body="The battery is new; the radio has been wrapped in a shirt to muffle it. A narrow strip of tape fixes the dial at the channel used before the order to leave.",anchor={scene="RBSWATStation"}},
-- T0306
{id="t0306-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The room nobody wanted",body="Thursday: the trial crew left their work shirts in the spare room. The sharp smell reached the kitchen, and the dog was sick before the road patrol arrived.",anchor={scene="RBSafehouse"}},
{id="t0306-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The extra occupant",body="They gave us a count for the beds and told us it was final. Then another family arrived at the back door with a child too tired to stand.\n\nWe made room and I put her shoes under the bed so nobody would trip. In the morning the list still had the old count. A visitor looked at the shoes and asked us to move them before the next inspection.\n\nThe child did not understand why her mother kept calling her by a different name. I did, but I did not tell her.",anchor={scene="RBSafehouse"}},
-- T0307
{id="t0307-01",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Two jars from the school garden",body="A cloudy water bottle and an empty sample jar share a strip of twine. Pale spray dust remains beneath both, inside the cupboard.",anchor={scene="RBSchool"}},
{id="t0307-02",kind="set",pieces={"Book","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Attendance from the wrong day",body="The roll book is open to an ordinary lesson. A pencil note on its back records a later head count, including pupils whose names are absent from the official list.",anchor={scene="RBSchool"}},
-- T0308
{id="t0308-01",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Soap bought after the field run",body="Soap, gloves, and two water jugs, paid cash. On the back: “Trial crew used the sink at dawn. My eyes burned before the road was shut.”",anchor={scene="RBShopLooted"}},
{id="t0308-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The inventory they took",body="The shelves were emptied twice. The first group took food; the second stepped over the broken glass to ask for the delivery ledger.\n\nI showed them the register because I had no ledger left. They wanted the names of people who had bought anything that morning. I could still recall one woman because her son carried the bag.\n\nThey wrote her down and told me not to mention their visit. I keep hearing the boy ask whether he could have the receipt.",anchor={scene="RBShopLooted"}},
-- T0309
{id="t0309-01",kind="set",pieces={"Mop","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The bucket with the bitter rinse",body="A mop has dried stiff across a bucket holding an oily film. The same film marks bootprints leading away from the kitchen shelf.",anchor={scene="RBSpiffo"}},
{id="t0309-02",kind="set",pieces={"DishCloth","Paperclip"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A clean counter and a missing roll",body="A fresh dish cloth lies under the register beside the empty spool where the morning receipts should be. Someone cleaned the counter after the rush, then removed only the record of it.",anchor={scene="RBSpiffo"}},
-- T0310
{id="t0310-01",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Photograph after the matinee",body="Written on the back: “The two men from the crop trial left yellow dust on every chair. We felt dizzy before the county van came.”",anchor={scene="RBStripclub"}},
{id="t0310-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The last table",body="I wrote the closing time on the chalkboard. Later a man asked me to rub it out and say we had shut earlier.\n\nThe people at the last table were still here when he came in. One of them had gone to call a friend and left a coat behind. I did not know whether to give the coat back when the man took their names.\n\nThe board is clean. The coat is in the cupboard with my own things. If anyone comes for it, I will tell them when I last saw its owner.",anchor={scene="RBStripclub"}},
-- T0311
{id="t0311-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","FirstAidKit"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Breakfast beside an unopened kit",body="A wrapped loaf and first-aid kit are tied together with road tape. Fine field dust covers the bread bag, but the kit is clean.",anchor={scene="RBTSBreakfast"}},
{id="t0311-02",kind="set",pieces={"Bowl","Spoon"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The missing breakfast tally",body="Two bowls are stacked around a folded scrap with a count written on it. The number served is larger than the number entered in the book, though the food has already been eaten.",anchor={scene="RBTSBreakfast"}},
-- T0312
{id="t0312-01",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Freezer note in a butcher's hand",body="I wrote down the sour smell after the field truck unloaded its rinse barrels. The meat was still cold when the flies vanished and the siren began.",anchor={scene="RBTSButcher"}},
{id="t0312-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A separate cut of meat",body="The shopkeeper made me bring the parcel through the back. He said the front counter was closed to anyone who had been beyond the roadblock.\n\nA visitor checked the wrapper but never asked what was inside. He took the slip with the customer name and left the parcel on the table. It began to drip while they argued about which list should keep the name.\n\nI washed the table when they left. The parcel was still there, and I could not decide whether throwing it away counted as a sale.",anchor={scene="RBTSButcher"}},
-- T0314
{id="t0314-01",kind="set",pieces={"Potato","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Supper left with a soil jar",body="A potato cut in half sits beside a jar of gray field water. Both carry the same waxy residue along the rim.",anchor={scene="RBTSDinner"}},
{id="t0314-02",kind="set",pieces={"Spoon","Bowl"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A cleared place setting",body="A spoon is laid across a bowl with a penciled count on its underside. The number is two higher than the count entered beside the meal.",anchor={scene="RBTSDinner"}},
-- T0315
{id="t0315-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The drink I poured away",body="I saved the bottle for you because it smelled like the trial orchard after spraying. I poured out the glasses before the roadblock appeared.",anchor={scene="RBTSDrink"}},
{id="t0315-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The drinks still owed",body="I put aside four glasses after the men came in. They said the others would be back for them and asked me to write the names on a napkin.\n\nI watched them pour the drinks away when they thought I had gone. The glasses were washed and returned to the shelf, but they kept the napkin.\n\nOne of the four had borrowed my coat. I still have the claim ticket for it, and no one will tell me where to take it.",anchor={scene="RBTSDrink"}},
-- T0316
{id="t0316-01",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Field radio with a fresh battery",body="A fresh battery is taped to a field radio. Green spray flecks fill the speaker grille, and the last tuning mark is below the county warning channel.",anchor={scene="RBTSElectronics"}},
{id="t0316-02",kind="set",pieces={"RadioBlack","Battery"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A receiver with a single mark",body="A radio sits beside a loose battery. A pencil mark on the dial matches one on the workbench; every other frequency has been scratched away.",anchor={scene="RBTSElectronics"}},
-- T0317
{id="t0317-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Recipe page, lower corner",body="My note says the farm crew washed their sample jars in this sink. The water turned milky; two hours later a patrol told us not to use the tap.",anchor={scene="RBTSFoodPreparation"}},
{id="t0317-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The missing cutting board",body="They told us to throw away the board but to leave the knife. I said we had served from both, and the man at the door asked only who had signed the delivery.\n\nMy helper had signed because I was late. She stayed behind to clean when they took the board. They asked for her address, then said she could go home.\n\nWe still have the order book. A page is gone, though the food from that order was already on the table.",anchor={scene="RBTSFoodPreparation"}},
-- T0318
{id="t0318-01",kind="set",pieces={"CannedCorn","Bandage"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Lunch wrapped with a bandage",body="A can of corn and sealed bandage are wrapped in the same strip of road tape. Yellow field dust is trapped under the tape.",anchor={scene="RBTSSandwich"}},
{id="t0318-02",kind="set",pieces={"Spoon","Paperclip"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="A sack beneath the sandwich tray",body="A spoon and a paperclip were caught in a folded feed sack used to line the tray. Its handwritten lot mark predates the closure notice pinned over it.",anchor={scene="RBTSSandwich"}},
-- T0319
{id="t0319-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Hemmed cuffs from the trial field",body="Friday: I mended three work shirts from the seed trial. White powder shook from every cuff; my hands blistered before anyone closed the road.",anchor={scene="RBTSSewing"}},
{id="t0319-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A sleeve sewn shut",body="The woman brought in a coat with its pocket torn. While I pinned it, a folded list fell out. She asked me to sew the pocket closed with the list inside.\n\nShe said her brother would need the coat if he returned. I offered to write his name on the label. She shook her head so hard she dropped the thread.\n\nI used a different color along the seam. If he comes back, someone can find the paper without ruining the whole coat.",anchor={scene="RBTSSewing"}},
-- T0320
{id="t0320-01",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","TinOpener"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Cloudy water beside the soup",body="A cloudy water bottle stands beside a tin opener crusted with yellow dust. A hand-drawn line on the bottle marks the level before boiling.",anchor={scene="RBTSSoup"}},
{id="t0320-02",kind="set",pieces={"Bowl","Spoon"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The unserved bowl",body="One bowl is clean and tied to a second with string. The count scratched into the first was reduced in pencil on the other, though both were carried to the table.",anchor={scene="RBTSSoup"}},
-- T0321
{id="t0321-01",kind="set",pieces={"Saw","Plank"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A repair set aside",body="The tools match a small repair, but the spare was prepared before anyone recorded a fault.",anchor={scene="RBTrashed"}},
{id="t0321-02",kind="set",pieces={"Bucket","HandShovel"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The spoiled pail",body="A bucket bears a faded field lot mark beneath a newer cleaning label. A hand shovel still has the same fine yellow dust caught in its handle.",anchor={scene="RBTrashed"}},
-- T0322
{id="t0322-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Thursday after closing — a sweet chemical smell",body="I saved the cloth with a sweet chemical smell for you. The water-treatment trial crew passed Thursday after closing; the rats left the shed, and afterward the clinic stopped answering.",anchor={scene="RBTwiggy"}},
{id="t0322-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The visitor at closing",body="A man sat by the back door and asked for the names of everyone who had come in. I assumed he meant the people still here.\n\nHe wanted the earlier customers too. I wrote down the one I knew because she brought her own mug. He crossed out her name, then asked whether I was certain she had arrived.\n\nHer mug is still under the counter. I have not washed it, though I cannot say what that proves.",anchor={scene="RBTwiggy"}},
-- T0323
{id="t0323-01",kind="set",pieces={"KeyRing","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Hand shovel and wash pail, friday before dawn",body="The hand shovel and wash pail share a bitter residue from the field-sprayer test. They were bundled before the radio warned everyone indoors.",anchor={scene="RBWoodcraft"}},
-- T0324
{id="t0324-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Saturday near lunch — a sharp solvent smell",body="Saturday near lunch: two workers from the crop plot carried a sharp solvent smell. two hens went still before the lane was closed.",anchor={scene="RDSBandPractice"}},
{id="t0324-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A rehearsal interrupted",body="We were halfway through the same song for the third time when a visitor came in and asked us to lower the volume. He needed to hear the radio in the hallway.\n\nThe voice on it was reading street names. One of us lived on the first street and went to call home. The visitor shut the door before the next name.\n\nWe tried to play again. Nobody could remember the first line, so I wrote the streets down instead.",anchor={scene="RDSBandPractice"}},
-- T0325
{id="t0325-01",kind="set",pieces={"FirstAidKit","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="First-aid kit and water bottle, sunday after supper",body="The first-aid kit and water bottle are tied together. blue powder coats one side; a torn strip of road tape covers the other.",anchor={scene="RDSBanditRaid"}},
{id="t0325-02",kind="set",pieces={"Map","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A folded address beside the raid",body="A map and a pencil are kept together in a pocket. Three homes have been circled, but only one has been crossed off; the mark was made before the door was forced.",anchor={scene="RDSBanditRaid"}},
-- T0326
{id="t0326-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="the night shift — white crystals",body="Personal note — the night shift: wash off the white crystals left by the livestock-feed study crew. the creek smelled wrong, and I had not yet heard that the siren began.",anchor={scene="RDSBathroomZed"}},
{id="t0326-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The names beyond the door",body="I heard someone knock while I was hiding here. He said he was checking the rooms and read a list aloud.\n\nThe name of the person with me was on it, though she had not told anyone we were here. She whispered that they had copied an older list from another building.\n\nHe left after we stayed quiet. I wrote the names I could remember so I can ask her later where that list came from.",anchor={scene="RDSBathroomZed"}},
-- T0327
{id="t0327-01",kind="set",pieces={"Potato","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Cut potato and sample jar, the early shift",body="The cut potato and sample jar share red grit from the fertilizer test. They were bundled before the buses quit running.",anchor={scene="RDSBedroomZed"}},
{id="t0327-02",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","Bandage"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A label under the pillow",body="A bottle of water and a strip of bandage have matching pencil marks. The marks are dates, not doses; someone was checking this bed before its occupant woke.",anchor={scene="RDSBedroomZed"}},
-- T0328
{id="t0328-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="the late afternoon — sticky pollen",body="I saved the cloth with sticky pollen for you. The orchard spray test crew passed the late afternoon; the mare refused her feed, and afterward the bridge was blocked.",anchor={scene="RDSBleach"}},
{id="t0328-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The count in a coat pocket",body="I asked for clean water. The man with the bucket asked how many people were still here before he opened it.\n\nI pointed to the room behind me. He wrote down a smaller number and said the others would be counted separately. He would not say where.\n\nThe bucket was emptied on the floor after he left. I kept the scrap he dropped because it has the number he first wrote.",anchor={scene="RDSBleach"}},
-- T0329
{id="t0329-01",kind="set",pieces={"Mop","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Mop and rinse bucket, the first hot day",body="The mop and rinse bucket share black specks from the pasture study. They were bundled before a patrol turned us back.",anchor={scene="RDSCorpsePsycho"}},
{id="t0329-02",kind="set",pieces={"Pencil","Sheet"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A folded list among the tools",body="A pencil and a torn sheet are folded together in a pocket. The sheet lists rooms by number, with the last two struck out in a different hand.",anchor={scene="RDSCorpsePsycho"}},
-- T0330
{id="t0330-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Monday morning — an oily film",body="Monday morning: two workers from the seed trial carried an oily film. my eyes began burning before the county van arrived.",anchor={scene="RDSDeadDrunk"}},
{id="t0330-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="After the music stopped",body="We thought he had fallen asleep and left him on the couch. A man at the door asked us to write down when we had last spoken to him.\n\nHe wanted one time for all of us. We disagreed because some of us had left the room. He wrote down his own time and asked us to sign below it.\n\nI still have the bottle cap he put beside the paper to hold it flat. I do not know whose account that paper is supposed to be.",anchor={scene="RDSDeadDrunk"}},
-- T0331
{id="t0331-01",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Battery and field radio, tuesday at dusk",body="The battery and field radio are tied together. green flecks coats one side; a torn strip of road tape covers the other.",anchor={scene="RDSDevouredByRats"}},
{id="t0331-02",kind="set",pieces={"Paperclip","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A count beneath the torn coat",body="The folded paper lists six arrivals and four departures. The pencil is tucked into the same pocket; two departures have been erased until the paper is almost transparent.",anchor={scene="RDSDevouredByRats"}},
-- T0332
{id="t0332-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Wednesday before rain — gray foam",body="Personal note — Wednesday before rain: wash off the gray foam left by the feed additive trial crew. my brother started coughing, and I had not yet heard that a deputy taped off the road.",anchor={scene="RDSFootballNight"}},
{id="t0332-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The score at halftime",body="At halftime we heard the street announcement through the open window. The others kept watching the game and I wrote the names of the roads on the back of the score sheet.\n\nSomeone came by after dark and asked me for it. He already knew the score and said he only wanted to check my spelling.\n\nI gave him the front half. The names are still here because I tore the page across the fold first.",anchor={scene="RDSFootballNight"}},
-- T0333
{id="t0333-01",kind="set",pieces={"Axe","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Hand axe and seed sack, thursday after closing",body="The hand axe and seed sack share milky water from the water-treatment trial. They were bundled before the clinic stopped answering.",anchor={scene="RDSGrouchos"}},
{id="t0333-02",kind="set",pieces={"DishCloth","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A cleaned pair of spectacles",body="A dish cloth is knotted around a water bottle. Inside it is a penciled count of people seen that afternoon, with one line altered after the cloth had been washed.",anchor={scene="RDSGrouchos"}},
-- T0334
{id="t0334-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Friday before dawn — yellow dust",body="I saved the cloth with yellow dust for you. The field-sprayer test crew passed Friday before dawn; three people felt dizzy, and afterward the radio warned everyone indoors.",anchor={scene="RDSGunmanInBathroom"}},
{id="t0334-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="What he said through the door",body="He told us to stay in the room and wait for the count. We could hear boots in the hall and someone asking whether to include the people behind the bathroom door.\n\nThe answer was no. They read out a number, then asked us to leave one at a time. He stayed behind with the door locked.\n\nI wrote the number down because it was smaller than the number of voices I had heard.",anchor={scene="RDSGunmanInBathroom"}},
-- T0335
{id="t0335-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","CannedCorn"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Wrapped loaf and canned corn, saturday near lunch",body="The wrapped loaf and canned corn share a sweet chemical smell from the crop plot. They were bundled before the lane was closed.",anchor={scene="RDSGunslinger"}},
{id="t0335-02",kind="set",pieces={"Map","DuctTape"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A second route in the pocket",body="The map is folded open to a road that has been erased in pencil. A strip of tape on the back carries the earlier route, preserved after the printed one was changed.",anchor={scene="RDSGunslinger"}},
-- T0336
{id="t0336-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Sunday after supper — a bitter residue",body="Sunday after supper: two workers from the greenhouse trial carried a bitter residue. my hands blistered before the phones went dead.",anchor={scene="RDSHenDo"}},
{id="t0336-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The list for the party",body="We put the guests names on a sheet so we could keep the surprise. A stranger arrived with a copy that had two names removed.\n\nHe asked whether those two had already left. I said one was still upstairs, getting ready. He folded his copy and waited at the foot of the stairs.\n\nNobody wanted to spoil the party by arguing. I have kept our list because it is the only one with everyone on it.",anchor={scene="RDSHenDo"}},
-- T0337
{id="t0337-01",kind="set",pieces={"Fertilizer","GardeningSprayEmpty"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fertilizer sack and empty sprayer, the night shift",body="The fertilizer sack and empty sprayer are tied together. a sharp solvent smell coats one side; a torn strip of road tape covers the other.",anchor={scene="RDSHockeyPsycho"}},
{id="t0337-02",kind="set",pieces={"Pencil","Paperclip"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A quiet inventory in a pocket",body="A notebook page is wrapped around a pencil. It counts three people at the door and four after it closed, with the extra tally squeezed into the margin.",anchor={scene="RDSHockeyPsycho"}},
-- T0338
{id="t0338-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="the early shift — blue powder",body="Personal note — the early shift: wash off the blue powder left by the fertilizer test crew. the dog refused its water, and I had not yet heard that the buses quit running.",anchor={scene="RDSHouseParty"}},
{id="t0338-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Someone took the guest book",body="We wrote names on the wall when the guest book disappeared. It was a joke until a visitor asked us to paint over them.\n\nOne friend had gone for more drinks and was not there to object. By morning somebody had covered only his name. The rest remained visible through the paint.\n\nI took a photograph before anyone did the second coat. I cannot tell if he came back while we were asleep.",anchor={scene="RDSHouseParty"}},
-- T0339
{id="t0339-01",kind="set",pieces={"HandShovel","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Hand shovel and wash pail, the late afternoon",body="The hand shovel and wash pail share white crystals from the orchard spray test. They were bundled before the bridge was blocked.",anchor={scene="RDSPokerNight"}},
{id="t0339-02",kind="set",pieces={"Pencil","Book"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="An empty seat at the table",body="A pencil lies through a ring of playing cards. The score sheet counts one more player than the chairs, and a later hand has rubbed the extra column thin.",anchor={scene="RDSPokerNight"}},
-- T0340
{id="t0340-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="the first hot day — red grit",body="I saved the cloth with red grit for you. The pasture study crew passed the first hot day; the flies vanished, and afterward a patrol turned us back.",anchor={scene="RDSPoliceAtHouse"}},
{id="t0340-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A number given at the door",body="They asked me to count the people inside while they were still walking through the house. I gave the number I knew.\n\nOne of them looked at a folded sheet and said it was too high. He asked whether a visitor had already gone home. The visitor was asleep upstairs.\n\nI left the number on the back of this envelope. If someone asks later, I want to remember what I actually saw.",anchor={scene="RDSPoliceAtHouse"}},
-- T0341
{id="t0341-01",kind="set",pieces={"FirstAidKit","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="First-aid kit and water bottle, monday morning",body="The first-aid kit and water bottle share sticky pollen from the seed trial. They were bundled before the county van arrived.",anchor={scene="RDSPrisonEscape"}},
{id="t0341-02",kind="set",pieces={"Map","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="An exit marked twice",body="A pencil and map share the same pocket. One route is marked toward the road, then overwritten with a line back toward the building.",anchor={scene="RDSPrisonEscape"}},
-- T0342
{id="t0342-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Tuesday at dusk — black specks",body="Tuesday at dusk: two workers from the pest-control test carried black specks. the garden browned before the checkpoint appeared.",anchor={scene="RDSPrisonEscapeWithPolice"}},
{id="t0342-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The names at the gate",body="We reached the gate before dawn. A man with a list asked us to give our names one at a time.\n\nWhen my companion spoke, the man stopped writing and looked at the person beside him. They argued over which list to use. We could see the road was clear.\n\nThey let the others through. We were told to wait for a second count, and I wrote the first count here so it would not disappear.",anchor={scene="RDSPrisonEscapeWithPolice"}},
-- T0343
{id="t0343-01",kind="set",pieces={"KeyRing","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Cut potato and sample jar, wednesday before rain",body="The cut potato and sample jar are tied together. an oily film coats one side; a torn strip of road tape covers the other.",anchor={scene="RDSRPGNight"}},
-- T0344
{id="t0344-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Thursday after closing — green flecks",body="Personal note — Thursday after closing: wash off the green flecks left by the water-treatment trial crew. the rats left the shed, and I had not yet heard that the clinic stopped answering.",anchor={scene="RDSRatInfested"}},
{id="t0344-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="How many traps were set",body="I counted the traps because I thought that was why they came. The visitor asked instead which doors we had opened that morning.\n\nHe marked one room as empty before looking in it. When I asked him to check again, he said the number had already been sent.\n\nThe traps remain. The door he marked empty is shut now, and I do not want to be the person who opens it.",anchor={scene="RDSRatInfested"}},
-- T0345
{id="t0345-01",kind="set",pieces={"Mop","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Mop and rinse bucket, friday before dawn",body="The mop and rinse bucket share gray foam from the field-sprayer test. They were bundled before the radio warned everyone indoors.",anchor={scene="RDSRatWar"}},
{id="t0345-02",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A corrected tally by the wall",body="A water bottle is tied to a pencil with string. The scratched tally on the bottle differs from the number copied onto the sheet beside it.",anchor={scene="RDSRatWar"}},
-- T0346
{id="t0346-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Saturday near lunch — milky water",body="I saved the cloth with milky water for you. The crop plot crew passed Saturday near lunch; two hens went still, and afterward the lane was closed.",anchor={scene="RDSResourceGarage"}},
{id="t0346-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The garage inventory",body="I told them which shelves had fuel and which held tools. They asked for the names of people who had filled containers the night before.\n\nI could remember the man who paid in coins because I had counted them twice. His number was already on their sheet. They did not ask me about the fuel after that.\n\nI put the coins away separately. The drawer still has the gap where the sheet had been kept.",anchor={scene="RDSResourceGarage"}},
-- T0347
{id="t0347-01",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Battery and field radio, sunday after supper",body="The battery and field radio share yellow dust from the greenhouse trial. They were bundled before the phones went dead.",anchor={scene="RDSSkeletonPsycho"}},
{id="t0347-02",kind="set",pieces={"Map","Rope"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A route folded into a pocket",body="The map is creased at the junction and tied with string. One destination has been erased so deeply that the paper nearly split; the route leading to it remains clear.",anchor={scene="RDSSkeletonPsycho"}},
-- T0348
{id="t0348-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="the night shift — a sweet chemical smell",body="the night shift: two workers from the livestock-feed study carried a sweet chemical smell. the creek smelled wrong before the siren began.",anchor={scene="RDSSpecificProfession"}},
{id="t0348-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The wrong occupation",body="The man writing the names asked what I did for a living. I told him, and he put down something else.\n\nHe said the form had no space for my work. I could see there was a space; it was already filled. The person beside me told me to let him finish.\n\nI wrote my own occupation here because I do not want the next person to think I lied about it.",anchor={scene="RDSSpecificProfession"}},
-- T0349
{id="t0349-01",kind="set",pieces={"Axe","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Hand axe and seed sack, the early shift",body="The hand axe and seed sack are tied together. a bitter residue coats one side; a torn strip of road tape covers the other.",anchor={scene="RDSStagDo"}},
{id="t0349-02",kind="set",pieces={"GlassTumbler","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The extra name on the score",body="A sheet and pencil are tucked under an empty glass. The guest count was changed after the first toast, but the marks around the glass show it had been there all night.",anchor={scene="RDSStagDo"}},
-- T0350
{id="t0350-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="the late afternoon — a sharp solvent smell",body="Personal note — the late afternoon: wash off the a sharp solvent smell left by the orchard spray test crew. the mare refused her feed, and I had not yet heard that the bridge was blocked.",anchor={scene="RDSStudentNight"}},
{id="t0350-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A list after the lights went out",body="We were supposed to be studying. When the lights failed, we counted everyone by calling out names across the room.\n\nA visitor came with a shorter list and said two people had gone home. One of them answered from the far corner. He crossed her name out anyway.\n\nShe wanted to leave then, but none of us knew whether the door was still open. I kept this page with her name on it.",anchor={scene="RDSStudentNight"}},
-- T0351
{id="t0351-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","CannedCorn"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Wrapped loaf and canned corn, the first hot day",body="The wrapped loaf and canned corn share blue powder from the pasture study. They were bundled before a patrol turned us back.",anchor={scene="RDSSuicidePact"}},
{id="t0351-02",kind="set",pieces={"Sheet","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A third mark on the page",body="A folded sheet and pencil are held beneath the same hand. Two names are boxed together, while a third is pressed into the paper hard enough to leave a mark without ink.",anchor={scene="RDSSuicidePact"}},
-- T0352
{id="t0352-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Monday morning — white crystals",body="I saved the cloth with white crystals for you. The seed trial crew passed Monday morning; my eyes began burning, and afterward the county van arrived.",anchor={scene="RDSTinFoilHat"}},
{id="t0352-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The person at the window",body="I made a hat to keep the rain off the radio. It looked ridiculous, so nobody noticed when I carried it from room to room.\n\nThe same street names came through three times. After the second reading a visitor told us the broadcast had never happened and asked for the radio.\n\nI took the battery out first. The station may be silent now, but I want to know what it says if it comes back.",anchor={scene="RDSTinFoilHat"}},
-- T0353
{id="t0353-01",kind="set",pieces={"Fertilizer","GardeningSprayEmpty"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fertilizer sack and empty sprayer, tuesday at dusk",body="The fertilizer sack and empty sprayer share red grit from the pest-control test. They were bundled before the checkpoint appeared.",anchor={scene="RDSZombieLockedBathroom"}},
{id="t0353-02",kind="set",pieces={"Pencil","Sheet"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A count through a locked door",body="A pencil and sheet are pushed beneath the door together. The sheet has an earlier head count, then a later number written over it without any sign the door was opened.",anchor={scene="RDSZombieLockedBathroom"}},
-- T0355
{id="t0355-01",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Coat pocket note — after Monday supper",body="My coat pocket entry says the well-water study workers brushed off silver specks. the mice abandoned the bin before the nurse stopped taking calls.",anchor={scene="RDSZombiesEating"}},
{id="t0355-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Four names, three bodies",body="I counted four names in the book they carried, but only three people lay here. The man with the book asked me not to look for the fourth.\n\nHe turned the page toward me to show that the missing person had already been accounted for. The writing was too small to read and he closed it before I could ask.\n\nI wrote the four names as well as I remember them. I may have misspelled one, but I know I heard it.",anchor={scene="RDSZombiesEating"}},
-- T0356
{id="t0356-01",kind="set",pieces={"Potato","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Cut potato with a soil jar at at Tuesday dawn",body="The cut potato with a soil jar are tied in one bundle. a greasy sheen marks the field side; torn warning tape marks the other.",anchor={scene="RVSAmbulanceCrash"}},
-- T0357
{id="t0357-01",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Cab note — late Wednesday",body="On the back: “late Wednesday, emerald flecks in the cab after the crop trial. the chickens stopped moving. Later, the back road closed.”",anchor={scene="RVSAnimalTrailerOnRoad"}},
-- T0358
{id="t0358-01",kind="set",pieces={"Mop","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Stiff mop with a rinse bucket at before Thursday lunch",body="The stiff mop with a rinse bucket carry brown foam from the greenhouse test. They were packed before the telephone line died.",anchor={scene="RVSBanditRoad"}},
